    "difficultyReason": "Heavily scaffolded: part (a) gives the target form, needing one use of the log quotient law and ln(e^{2x}) = 2x. Part (b) says 'hence', so the student differentiates 2x - ln(1+e^x) by the chain rule and combines over a common denominator to reach the given result. There are two or three linked routine steps and no hidden insight, so it is a little easier than the 30-level references.",
